[Income-tax Act, 1961 | Chapter X: SPECIAL PROVISIONS RELATING TO AVOIDANCE OF TAX | Section 99: Treatment of connected person and accommodating party. | regime=current | effective 1962-04-01 to present]
99. Treatment of connected person and accommodating party. —For the purposes of this Chapter, in determining whether a tax benefit exists,—( i ) the parties who are connected persons in relation to each other may be treated as one and the same person;
( ii ) any accommodating party may be disregarded;
( iii ) the accommodating party and any other party may be treated as one and the same person;
( iv ) the arrangement may be considered or looked through by disregarding any corporate structure.

